    "description": "Rotation subsystem (full-parity R3, the capstone — P0+feature+repeat). A rotation is a tree of nodes composing already-gated per-hit DAMAGE features into a sequence; its rotation.total output is THREE independent componentwise accumulators (Tree.js:36-44,110-136): total_normal=Σ count·perFeatureNormal, total_crit=Σ count·perFeatureCrit, total_average=Σ count·perFeatureAverage (each hit blended AT ITS OWN crit rate, THEN summed — NEVER blend(total_normal,total_crit) at one rate). build.setRotation(new DB.__Rotation({items})) (CalcSet.js:173) → getFeaturesList calls compileRotation() (CalcSet.js:453-459) → getFeaturesHash keys it rotation.total → FeatureRotation.getResult dumps a normal {normal,crit,average} triple (category rotation). 4 reps: rotation-fischl-mixed-crit (Fischl, enemy_weak_shot ON: charged_aimed [electro AIMED → 100% crit] + normal_hit_1×5 [physical → ~5% crit] — the crit rates DIFFER, so avg=blend(Σnormal,Σcrit) fails: THE mixed-crit guard) / rotation-keqing-simple (Keqing normal_hit_1×3, a simple count>1 sequence) / rotation-fischl-repeat (repeat ×3 of [normal_hit_1] — repeated block == 3× single) / rotation-fischl-mixed-block (charged_aimed + repeat×2[normal_hit_1] + aimed, weak_shot ON — reorderItems defers the repeat after loose features but the SUM is order-independent). rotationBurndown reconstructs each spec from partyRecord.rotation, compiles via compileRotation, asserts rotation.total normal/crit/avg within 0.1.",
